# Pirate WebArcade — vendored game sources (pinned).
#
# These games are third-party works we redistribute; we do NOT modify their
# code. Each row pins exactly where the bytes came from so the import is
# reproducible and attributable.
#
# Format (tab-separated, '#' comments and blank lines ignored):
#   id  license  kind  repo  ref  subpath  bundle  dest
#
#   id       short stable id (also the PirateArcadeGames id)
#   license  SPDX-ish license label (documentation only)
#   kind     "repo" -> bundle = dist/ folder inside the repo archive
#            "zip"  -> bundle = a standalone zip download (e.g. js13k entry)
#   repo     owner/name, ALWAYS set (used to fetch LICENSE text)
#   ref      git commit sha for repo/kind; a date/note for zip (documentation)
#   subpath  for kind=repo, the folder inside the archive to copy
#   bundle   for kind=zip, the url to download; "-" for kind=repo
#   dest     folder under Resources/_Pirate/WebUI/Arcade/
#
# To refresh: run Scripts/sh/vendor-arcade-games.sh (optionally: <id> ...).
# The script writes PROVENANCE.txt + LICENSE.txt into each dest; commit both.

